  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "The chain",
   "items": [
    "Spatial correlation leads to simultaneous generation, which depresses the price, which lowers the capture rate and revenue",
    "Correlation is computed on deviations from the clear-sky profile; raw output correlates near 0.95 only because the sun rises everywhere",
    "The decay length L is estimated by season: diversification is expected to fail under winter blocking highs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "violet",
   "title": "Strategy",
   "items": [
    "Capacity shares from the cleaned covariance, with expected capture rate in place of expected return",
    "Five arms scored identically, from equal weight to the capture-rate objective",
    "Equal weight is expected to be competitive and is reported as such"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "slate",
   "title": "Data and credit",
   "items": [
    "Weather: ERA5 (Hersbach et al. 2020), a reanalysis with known cloud biases. Prices: ENTSO-E",
    "Capture rate follows the value-factor framing of Hirth (2013)",
    "Cleaning, effective rank, tail dependence and loadings are imported from corrlib"
   ]
  }
